<title>GERMANY: Linde interested in Messer Griesheim-report.</title>
<headline>Linde interested in Messer Griesheim-report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German plant and engineering group Linde AG is interested in taking over Messer Griesheim, a unit of chemicals giant Hoechst AG, the Platow Brief newsletter reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>In an advance release of its Monday edition, Platow said Linde did not have concrete takeover plans, but viewed Messer Griesheim, a producer of industrial gases, as a suitable candidate. The report cited sources close to Linde.</p>
<p>Hoechst has said in the past it wants to float Messer Griesheim. Linde was not available for comment.</p>
<p>((-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525))</p>
